title: IainSchweblinClue0
---
In the middle of a cold winter night, a prepubescent Iain awoke to a strange sound coming from his closet. This cacophony of clicking slowly began to fill his awareness as he came to from his deep sleep. Finding the closet as the culprit, he slowly got up and open the door to see a swarm of termites feasting on the closet. Their translucent bodies and sharp pincers scurried erratically up and down the walls. The wall was covered in rows of tiny holes, an uncanny pattern. Iain jumped back, shaking and batting at his arms. He could feel the termites crawling up his skin and the vision of their creation haunted him. He ran out of his room screaming.
===

title: IainSchweblinClue1
---
Iain wasn’t the most popular kid at Morrison Middle School. He didn’t talk much and, when he did, he couldn’t seem to find a way to fit the words together into a coherent sentence. He got picked on by a couple of paunchy older kids. One particularly cruel lunch period, Iain opened his lunch box to find three large beetles laying waste to his sandwich. He threw it to the floor and ran away screaming. The two boys laughed at him until their gut fell out of their pants. Iain never saw that lunch box again and vowed to stay far away from lively gardens.
===
title: IainSchweblinClue2
---
Like most kids, Iain didn’t love going to the doctor. The harsh white lights and creepy old nurses made him dread the twenty minute drive to the pediatrician. One year, Iain had to get some blood work done. A young assistant came in to take his blood. He sat in his mother’s lap while the assistant prepared the needle and vile. He closed his eyes as she pressed the needle into his skin. He try to zone out from the whole thing until he heard the words “all done”. Opening his eyes, all he saw was blood shooting up out of the wound and covered the young women. She pressed her palm against it while she struggled to bandage it up. The sight of her face covered in blood scarred him. Iain still thinks about it every time he has to go to the doctor. 
===